The tests call `proverb(*input_data, qualifier=None)` and return a list of lines. Implementation:

```python
def proverb(*pieces, qualifier=None):
    lines = []
    for current, consequence in zip(pieces, pieces[1:]):
        lines.append(f"For want of a {current} the {consequence} was lost.")
    if pieces:
        first = pieces[0]
        if qualifier:
            lines.append(f"And all for the want of a {qualifier} {first}.")
        else:
            lines.append(f"And all for the want of a {first}.")
    return lines
```

